        "reason": "The evidence states the authors propose a method to automatically generate labeled NER datasets using DBpedia and Wikipedia, and describe the work as constructing a 'massive, weakly-supervised dataset (i.e. a silver standard corpora).' The dataset (SESAME) is generated automatically without manual annotation, though it is weakly/silver-standard (labels derived automatically rather than gold human annotation), so it is automatically generated rather than completely human-annotated."
